---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Postcard } from '../components/Postcard';
import { demoPortfolio } from '../lib/demo';
---

<Layout
  title="Crypto portfolio tracker, with perspective | CryptoPatro"
  description="Track your crypto without connecting a wallet. See your mix, understand your numbers, and share a portfolio postcard. Free, open source, by Doruk Gezici."
>
  <div class="public-shell">
    <header class="public-nav">
      <a class="brand" href="/">
        <img src="/favicon.svg" width="34" height="34" alt="" />
        <span>
          cryptopatro<span class="brand-dot">.</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <nav class="public-nav-actions" aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a class="about-nav-github" href="https://github.com/dorukgezici/CryptoPatro">
          Open source ↗
        </a>
        <a class="button primary" href="/?start=1">
          Make it yours <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </nav>
    </header>
    <main id="main">
      <section class="public-hero">
        <div class="eyebrow">
          <span class="status-dot"></span> A CALMER CORNER OF CRYPTO
        </div>
        <h1>
          Your crypto.
          <br />A little <span>clearer.</span>
        </h1>
        <p>
          A personal portfolio tracker for people who want perspective, not another screen to stare
          at. See what you own. Understand your mix. Get on with your day.
        </p>
        <a class="button primary" href="/?start=1">
          Start with one holding <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <div class="about-proof">
          <span>✓ Free and open source</span>
          <span>✓ No exchange keys</span>
          <span>✓ No signup to get started</span>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="about-visual">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">YOUR PERSPECTIVE, BEAUTIFULLY PACKED</div>
          <h2>
            A portfolio is personal.
            <br />
            Your balance can stay that way.
          </h2>
          <p>
            Turn your allocation into a little postcard. Share your perspective with a friend, or
            the internet. Your quantities, balance, and cost basis stay behind.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/?share=1">
            Try a sample postcard <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <Postcard allocation={demoPortfolio.allocation} isDemo={true} source="sample" />
      </section>
      <section class="about-columns" aria-label="How it works">
        <article>
          <div class="about-step">01 / A CLEARER PICTURE</div>
          <h2>Start with what you own.</h2>
          <p>
            Add an asset, its quantity, and your average buy price. Your private workspace shows its
            value, cost basis, and estimated price movement in one place.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div class="about-step">02 / A LITTLE CONTEXT</div>
          <h2>Understand the bigger picture.</h2>
          <p>
            See where your portfolio is concentrated. Ask Patro to explain the numbers in plain
            language. Set a target price and check it when you come back.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div class="about-step">03 / A SHARED PERSPECTIVE</div>
          <h2>Pass something useful on.</h2>
          <p>
            Make a postcard of your mix. Share a public link or save an image. Every postcard gives
            the next person a simple way to build their own.
          </p>
        </article>
      </section>
      <section class="methodology" id="methodology">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">NO BLACK BOXES</div>
          <h2>Good perspective starts with honest numbers.</h2>
          <p>Here’s exactly what you’re looking at, and what this first release does.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <details open>
            <summary>Where do the prices come from?</summary>
            <p>
              CoinGecko provides indicative USD quotes and seven-day price history for Bitcoin,
              Ethereum, Solana, USDC, Avalanche, and Chainlink. Quotes are cached briefly. If the
              provider is unavailable, the app labels cached or illustrative sample prices and shows
              their timestamp. Sample data is never described as live.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>How are returns and charts calculated?</summary>
            <p>
              Value is quantity multiplied by the latest quote. Unrealized profit compares that
              value with your entered average buy price. Returns are hidden when cost basis is
              unknown. The chart revalues your current quantities at past prices. It is a
              hypothetical view, not your actual account history. Fees, sells, taxes, and realized
              returns are not tracked.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Where is my portfolio saved?</summary>
            <p>
              Your holdings are saved on the server. A private bearer key in this browser provides
              access. No wallet access or exchange credentials are needed. Clearing browser storage
              loses that key. This release does not include account recovery, cross-device sync, or
              exchange imports.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Is Patro really AI?</summary>
            <p>
              When an AI provider is configured by the host, Pydantic AI interprets your question
              and the server answers with verified portfolio calculations. Otherwise Patro provides
              a clearly labeled local portfolio summary. It does not predict prices or place trades.
              Each question is independent, and portfolio context is educational.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What happens when I create a postcard?</summary>
            <p>
              You choose a title and whether to include a return percentage. The public snapshot
              contains asset names and allocation percentages, never balances, quantities, cost
              basis, or your access key. Anyone with its link can view it. Personal postcards can be
              revoked from the share dialog. Demo postcards are public samples. Basic share and
              referral events help understand how the product is discovered, without recording
              portfolio values or browser identifiers.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>How do price alerts work?</summary>
            <p>
              Alerts are checked when you open the price alerts screen or select “Check prices.”
              Only fresh provider quotes can trigger an alert. They are in-app checks, not
              background notifications. Email, push, and Telegram delivery are not part of this
              release.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="about-maker">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">A SMALL, INDEPENDENT PROJECT</div>
          <h2>Built by Doruk Gezici.</h2>
          <p>
            CryptoPatro began as a personal crypto tracking project. This is its next chapter: an
            open-source tool that makes the numbers easier to live with. Follow the build, read the
            code, or help shape what comes next.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a
          class="button secondary"
          href="https://github.com/dorukgezici"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >
          Meet the maker <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="public-footer">
      <span>© {new Date().getFullYear()} CryptoPatro. A perspective, not investment advice.</span>
      <a href="/">
        Explore the sample portfolio <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </footer>
  </div>
</Layout>
